# 3D Blog Project - Glassmorphism Design System Rules

## 🎨 Glassmorphism Design System

### Core Principles
- Use existing glassmorphism utility classes from `src/shared/lib/glassmorphism-plugin.ts`
- Maintain consistency across all UI components
- Apply glassmorphism effects through Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Ensure proper layering with z-index and backdrop-blur

### Available Glassmorphism Classes

#### Basic Glass Effects
- `.bg-glass` - Basic glassmorphism background
- `.glass-card` - Standard glass card with hover effects
- `.glass-card-static` - Static glass card without animations
- `.glass-card-float-shimmer` - Floating glass card with shimmer animation

#### Button Variants
- `.btn-glass` - Standard glass button with white/transparent styling
- `.btn-glass-primary` - Primary glass button with blue accent
- `.btn-glass-secondary` - Secondary glass button with purple accent
- `.btn-glass-success` - Success glass button with green accent
- `.btn-glass-warning` - Warning glass button with yellow accent
- `.btn-glass-danger` - Danger glass button with red accent

#### Colored Glass Cards
- `.glass-blue-float` - Blue-tinted floating glass card
- `.glass-purple-float` - Purple-tinted floating glass card
- `.glass-green-float` - Green-tinted floating glass card
- `.glass-red-float` - Red-tinted floating glass card

#### Special Effects
- `.glass-shimmer` - Adds shimmer animation to glass elements
- `.glass-glow-blue` - Blue glow effect for glass elements
- `.glass-glow-purple` - Purple glow effect for glass elements

### Implementation Guidelines

#### 1. Component Integration
```tsx
// ✅ Correct - Use existing utility classes
<Button variant="glass">Glass Button</Button>
<Card className="glass-card-float-shimmer">Content</Card>

// ❌ Avoid - Creating custom glassmorphism styles
<div className="bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/20">
```

#### 2. Component Variants

##### Button Components
- **Custom Button** (`src/shared/ui/Button/Button.tsx`):
  ```tsx
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'comment' | 'reply' | 'glass' | 'glass-primary'
  ```
- **Shadcn Button** (`src/shadcn-ui/components/ui/button.tsx`):
  ```tsx
  variant: 'glass' | 'glass-primary'
  ```

##### Tag Components
- **Tag Component** (`src/shared/ui/Tag/tag.tsx`):
  ```tsx
  type?: 'solid' | 'glass' | 'outline' | 'gradient'
  color?: 'blue' | 'purple' | 'green' | 'red' | 'yellow' | 'pink' | 'cyan' | ...
  ```

##### DropdownMenu Components
- **DropdownMenu** uses `.glass-card` utility class
- **DropdownMenuItem** has custom glassmorphism hover effects

#### 3. Layering and Z-Index Rules
```css
/* Z-Index Hierarchy */
z-[9999] - Tooltips (highest priority)
z-50     - Modal overlays
z-40     - Dropdown menus
z-30     - Floating elements
z-20     - Glass cards with shimmer
z-10     - Standard glass cards
z-0      - Base elements
```

#### 4. Animation Guidelines
- Use `.glass-shimmer` for subtle shimmer effects
- Apply `glass-card-float-shimmer` for premium card components
- Shimmer animations should have 4s duration with ease-in-out timing
- Hover effects should include scale transformations (1.02-1.05)

#### 5. Color System Integration
```tsx
// Glass backgrounds should match color tokens
glassColorStyles = {
  blue: 'bg-blue-500/10 backdrop-blur-md border border-blue-400/30 text-blue-200',
  purple: 'bg-purple-500/10 backdrop-blur-md border border-purple-400/30 text-purple-200',
  // ... other colors
}
```

### Development Workflow

#### 1. Before Adding New Glassmorphism Styles
1. Check `src/shared/lib/glassmorphism-plugin.ts` for existing utilities
2. Use existing classes when possible
3. Only extend the plugin for new, reusable patterns

#### 2. Component Updates
1. Always prefer existing glassmorphism variants over custom styles
2. Update both custom and shadcn components when adding new variants
3. Test glassmorphism effects across different themes (light/dark)

#### 3. Performance Considerations
- Use `backdrop-filter: blur()` sparingly to maintain performance
- Prefer static glass effects over animated ones for large lists
- Apply `will-change: transform` for animated glass elements

