### Common Patterns

#### Glass Card with Content
```tsx
<Card className="glass-card-float-shimmer">
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Glass Card Title</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>
    Content goes here
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

#### Glass Button Group
```tsx
<div className="flex gap-2">
  <Button variant="glass" size="sm">Cancel</Button>
  <Button variant="glass-primary" size="sm">Confirm</Button>
</div>
```

#### Glass Tag Collection
```tsx
<div className="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
  <Tag type="glass" color="blue">React</Tag>
  <Tag type="glass" color="purple">TypeScript</Tag>
  <Tag type="glass" color="green">Node.js</Tag>
</div>
```

### Debugging Guidelines

#### Common Issues
1. **Shimmer not visible**: Check if parent has `overflow: hidden`
2. **Blur effect clipped**: Ensure adequate padding/margin around glass elements
3. **Z-index conflicts**: Follow the established z-index hierarchy
4. **Performance issues**: Reduce number of backdrop-blur elements

#### Testing Checklist
- [ ] Glass effects work in both light and dark themes
- [ ] Hover states provide appropriate feedback
- [ ] Animations are smooth and not janky
- [ ] Elements are properly layered (z-index)
- [ ] Mobile responsiveness maintained
- [ ] Accessibility standards met (focus states, contrast)

### Best Practices

#### Do's ✅
- Use consistent glassmorphism classes across the project
- Apply glass effects to enhance UI hierarchy
- Test glassmorphism effects across different backgrounds
- Maintain proper contrast ratios for accessibility
- Use subtle animations that enhance UX

#### Don'ts ❌
- Don't create inline glassmorphism styles
- Don't overuse shimmer effects (can be distracting)
- Don't apply glassmorphism to every element
- Don't ignore performance implications of backdrop-filter
- Don't sacrifice accessibility for visual effects

### Future Considerations
- Monitor browser support for backdrop-filter
- Consider fallbacks for older browsers
- Evaluate performance impact on mobile devices
- Plan for potential CSS-in-JS migration
- Maintain consistency with design system evolution
